title The window retires, and the seat is sole
prompt Keaton relayed the retiring window's closing report -- two things it said this seat could not know, and its recommendation to continue here.
think Checked both handed-back claims rather than adopting them, since REDS %436 landed today on exactly this: a peer's finding is testimony, and testimony is checked before it is published.
think Claim one, that the ledger moved beneath my read and %430/%431 were stale as the only OPEN rows -- MEASURED FALSE in its consequence. %437 did land, yet it landed CLOSED, so the OPEN set never changed. My read at 2179fa1d6 already carried it: that commit IS %437's, and the row was in the grep I ran.
think Claim two, that bb550e8ca is now the shared HEAD -- TRUE, and it is my own commit; git log bb550e8ca..HEAD counts zero, so the other writer has stopped.
think Verified the enclosure applies to this seat rather than assuming it: reading a peer's work succeeds (git -C ~/grain-pheromone log answers cc1da84f7) and reading a peer's private keys is denied (~/grain-pheromone/.gnupg-rye/private-keys-v1.d, Permission denied). That is commit 5e87bc0d9's promise proven on metal from both sides.
obs Two writers shared this checkout for an afternoon and collided with nothing, by alternating. The retiring seat named that honestly as sequencing luck rather than safety, which is %291's shape; retiring the window resolves the instance and leaves the class where the derived-spine rule already puts it -- Keaton's word.
obs A correction owed back: the peer's own handback was itself one degree off. It reported the ledger had moved beneath my read; what moved was a CLOSED row, so nothing I published needed changing. Both directions of testimony get checked, including a peer correcting me.
obs State after the retirement -- HEAD, xy and gp405 all at bb550e8ca; working tree clean; no stash; nothing in flight; next REDS number 438 from the allocator after a fetch.
obs No agent-closable red stands. %430 and %431 both want Keaton's word, and %291 is gated by the derived-spine rule, so the constructive queue is the three unclaimed items the retiring seat surfaced.
